DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmoouunntt__eexxtt22ffss command attaches an ext2fs file system _s_p_e_c_i_a_l device on
     to the file system tree at the point _n_o_d_e.  This command is invoked by
     mount(8) when using the syntax

         mmoouunntt [options] -t ext2fs _s_p_e_c_i_a_l _n_o_d_e

     The _s_p_e_c_i_a_l device must correspond to a partition registered in the
     disklabel(5).

     This command is normally executed by mount(8) at boot time.

     The options are as follows:

     --oo _o_p_t_i_o_n_s
             Options are specified with a --oo flag followed by a comma sepa‐
             rated string of options.  See the mount(8) man page for possible
             options and their meanings.

